# =============================================================================
# USING OTHER MODELS (examples - all commented out)
# =============================================================================
# The two CHAT roles (REASONING and NON_REASONING) work with any
# OpenAI-compatible API: local models, OpenAI, Claude, Gemini, OpenRouter.
# This needs LLM_CLIENT=openai (a local patch in auto_ontology/utils/llm_invoke.py).
#
# EMBED and RERANK must stay on NVIDIA (cloud, or a self-hosted NIM):
#   - the vector column in Postgres is fixed at 2048 dimensions
#     (OpenAI = 1536/3072, Gemini = 3072, Amazon Titan v2 = up to 1024)
#   - every embedding request sends NVIDIA-only fields (input_type, truncate)
# So Gemini, OpenAI or Titan embeddings need code changes. Chat models do not.
#
# To switch: uncomment ONE block, run `docker compose up -d`, then rebuild
# the ontology in Settings → Semantic Compilation. No need to re-ingest.
# [tested] = run against the app's real prompts on 2026-11-08.

# --- Local model with Ollama (free, private) [tested: llama3.1:8b] ---
# Run `ollama pull llama3.1:8b` first. host.docker.internal = your own machine.
# LLM_CLIENT=openai
# REASONING_ENDPOINT=http://host.docker.internal:11434/v1
# REASONING_MODEL=llama3.1:8b
# REASONING_API_KEY=ollama
# NON_REASONING_ENDPOINT=http://host.docker.internal:11434/v1
# NON_REASONING_MODEL=llama3.1:8b
# NON_REASONING_API_KEY=ollama

# --- OpenRouter: one key for GPT, Claude and Gemini [tested] ---
# Tested: openai/gpt-5.6-luna, anthropic/claude-opus-5.5,
#         google/gemini-3.8-flash, google/gemini-2.5-pro
# LLM_CLIENT=openai
# REASONING_ENDPOINT=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
# REASONING_MODEL=anthropic/claude-opus-5.5
# REASONING_API_KEY=sk-or-your-openrouter-key
# NON_REASONING_ENDPOINT=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
# NON_REASONING_MODEL=google/gemini-3.8-flash
# NON_REASONING_API_KEY=sk-or-your-openrouter-key

# --- OpenAI directly [same model tested via OpenRouter] ---
# LLM_CLIENT=openai
# REASONING_ENDPOINT=https://api.openai.com/v1
# REASONING_MODEL=gpt-5.6-luna
# REASONING_API_KEY=sk-your-openai-key
# NON_REASONING_ENDPOINT=https://api.openai.com/v1
# NON_REASONING_MODEL=gpt-5.6-luna
# NON_REASONING_API_KEY=sk-your-openai-key

# --- Claude directly, via Anthropic's OpenAI-compatible endpoint ---
# [same model tested via OpenRouter]
# LLM_CLIENT=openai
# REASONING_ENDPOINT=https://api.anthropic.com/v1/
# REASONING_MODEL=claude-opus-5-5
# REASONING_API_KEY=sk-ant-your-anthropic-key
# NON_REASONING_ENDPOINT=https://api.anthropic.com/v1/
# NON_REASONING_MODEL=claude-haiku-5-5
# NON_REASONING_API_KEY=sk-ant-your-anthropic-key

# --- Gemini directly, via Google's OpenAI-compatible endpoint ---
# [same models tested via OpenRouter]
# LLM_CLIENT=openai
# REASONING_ENDPOINT=https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/openai/
# REASONING_MODEL=gemini-2.5-pro
# REASONING_API_KEY=your-gemini-api-key
# NON_REASONING_ENDPOINT=https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/openai/
# NON_REASONING_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash
# NON_REASONING_API_KEY=your-gemini-api-key

# --- Amazon Bedrock (Mantle endpoint) [not tested] ---
# Bedrock's "Mantle" endpoint speaks the OpenAI Chat Completions API.
# Use a Bedrock API key (Bedrock console -> API keys).
# Works for open-weight models (gpt-oss, Qwen, DeepSeek, Mistral...).
# NOT for Claude (Messages API only on Mantle) or GPT-5.x (Responses API
# only) - for Claude use the "Claude direct" block, or a LiteLLM gateway.
# Check the AWS "endpoint availability by model" page for your region.
# REASONING_ENDPOINT=https://bedrock-mantle.us-east-1.api.aws/v1
# REASONING_API_KEY=your-bedrock-api-key
# REASONING_MODEL=openai.gpt-oss-120b
# NON_REASONING_ENDPOINT=https://bedrock-mantle.us-east-1.api.aws/v1
# NON_REASONING_API_KEY=your-bedrock-api-key
# NON_REASONING_MODEL=openai.gpt-oss-20b
